---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import Problem from "../components/Problem.astro";
import Checks from "../components/Checks.astro";
import Report from "../components/Report.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Page
  title="How it works — Aethens"
  description="Why verifier bugs matter, what checks C001–C007 can and cannot catch, and a real Aethens report."
>
  <section class="border-b border-line" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
    <div class="wrap py-16 sm:py-20">
      <p class="kicker mb-5"><span>How it works</span></p>
      <h1 id="how-heading" class="font-serif italic font-semibold text-section leading-[1.1] max-w-3xl">
        A CLI and a GitHub Action that run the verifier.
      </h1>
      <div class="mt-6 max-w-2xl space-y-4 text-paper/90">
        <p>
          Aethens is an open-source Python CLI and GitHub Action that audits the verifiers of RL
          environments and code-task benchmarks by running them in a Docker sandbox. Every finding
          comes with evidence and a one-line repro command. The checks themselves have published
          precision and recall you can reproduce.
        </p>
        <p>
          v0.1.0 is on PyPI. No LLMs, no network access for task code, no telemetry, no hosted
          service yet. Install instructions are on the
          <a class="prose-link" href={`${base}docs/`}>docs</a> page. The Action is documented
          separately.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Problem />
  <Checks />
  <Report />
</Page>
